TheTis a literal to separate the date from the time.

AnPlainDateTime objectcan be created in several different ways:

You can create aPlainDateTime objectusing thenewconstructor.

The constructor takesparameterslike year, month, day, hours, and minutes.

You can create aPlainDateTime objectfrom anISO 8601 / RFC 9557 string.

TheTis a literal to separate the date from the time.

You should read it as an abbreviation forTime.

It is the separator required by theISO 8601 format.

You can create aPlainDateTime objectfrom current time.

You can safely add or subtract time.

The original value does not change.

You cancomparePlaneDateTime values using theequals()method.

Most (*) temporal objectshave their ownequals() method:

(*) Duration has not.

A PlainDateTime object does not include time zone information.

You canconvertit to aZonedDateTimeif needed.

TheTemporal.PlainDateTime objecthas22 propertiesof date information.

### Code Snippets

```
// Create a PlainDateTime object
const dateTime = Temporal.PlainDateTime.from("2026-05-17T14:30:00");

---

// Create a PlainDateTime object
const date = new Temporal.PlainDateTime(2026, 5, 17, 14, 30);

---

// Create a PlainDateTime object
